        <p>COPY OF ANALYST'S REPORT.</p>
        <p>OWEN SIMMONS, F.C.S., Bread and Flour Analyst.</p>
        <p>360, Coldharbour Lane,</p>
        <p>Brixton, London, S.W., October, 1906.</p>
        <p>CERTIFICATE OF QUALITY AND PURITY.</p>
        <p>" I am duly in receipt of two loaves from Messrs. Toft, 98, Bridge Street, Warrington, and after el.chaustive examination aud analyses, have pleasure in certifying that I find them to be (t) of very excellent general quality ; (2) particularly digestible, nutritious and of good flavour; (3) skilfully and carefully manufactured from the best class materials throughout ; (4) worth, both dietetically and commercially, the highest current price of the day, being relatively cheaper than the so-called cheap, but inferior qualities sometimes supplied ; (5) absolutely pure and worthy of the highest recommendation to those who desire good health, and who too often forget that the best and most desirable materials cannot be sold by anyone at the same price as those of lower quality ; and finally (6) to be, as already indicated, of such high quality as would obtain distinction at any Bread Exhibition or Competition."</p>
        <p>(Signed),</p>
        <p>OWEN SIMMONS, F.C.S. _</p>
        <p>DELIVERIES IN ALL PARTS OF TOWN DAILY.</p>
