      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-10-27_WidnesExaminer_art0037" n="art0037">
        <head>TO-DAY'S' RF,CirE.</head>
        <p>TO-DAY'S' RF,CirE.</p>
        <p>Wm 4 ) Oreg.—'u+ Soz. Of 'fattter in a nisith loz. of flour. Stir them together ~,tAaLwMplag OF until it becomes a nice brown. Add by degrees, half a tumbler of very good stock and the same quantity of red wine. two witofo shallots. a bunch of herbs and a bay leaf, peprer and a little salt, and put in. the bones -and bcdy of the bird, from which you have taken all the 'meat. Let all Oii. boil gently together for half-anAiour, then strai, t. through a cot:inkier uno put Inc gravy back in the stewpan, and just when on the point of boil- ing put in all the pieces ,of bird. Toast a round of bread, cut it into four piK!es, lay them at the bottom of a very hot dish, arrange the bird on them, pour the gravy over, which ought to be nice and, thick, and garnish with slices of lemon.</p>
