      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-10-27_WidnesExaminer_art0045" n="art0045">
        <head>Fish's Record Score.</head>
        <p>Fish's Record Score.</p>
        <p>Wan Ington renewed accpiaintance with Huddersfield on Saturday and 5,000 spectato:s w;tnessed a reirark- able game. The home team played brilliant football and pat on the huge scons of 10 goals, 10 tries (50 points) to a try. Huddersfield were somewhat weakened by the abse see of Sutcliffe, Davies, Kitchen, and Patchett but th 3 sabstitutes gave a good account of thems Aces. 'me weather was fine and the ground in splendid condstion. Teams . Warrpington—C3rry, back ; Fish, Isherwood, Taylor, and Jordan, t'lree-quarter backs : Eiockenhall and Lees, half backs ; Preston, Boardm Harmer, Heath,Thomas and Belton, forwards.</p>
        <p>_ Huddersfield—thrtholomew, back ; Wade, Mosley, Garside and Ainley, three-quarter backs ; Hockins and Jagger, half backs ; Wilson, Cole, Langthorne, Brook, Hirst and CSarlesworth forwards.</p>
        <p>Referee, Mr. H. Edraundson,Bradford. Touch judges, Messrs. J.Edwards (St.Helens)and E. Pearson, (Leigh.) The home men soon got on the attack, and from a cross kick by Isherwood, Bartholomew failed to field and Boardman rushed over between the posts, Fish placing a goal. Huddersfield rallied, and a brilliant, run by Wade and subsequent pass to Langthorne ended in a try to the Huddersfield forward. The game con- tinued to be splendidly contested, and fine work by Wade constantly harased the home defence. As the game progressed Warrington improved, and a capital move- ment by Isherwood and Fish led up to Thomas scoring. Huddersfield were next penalised, and Fish placed a goal, and a moment later he crossed the visitor's line, also adding the goal. Near the interval another round of passing by the home back sanded in Taylor scoring and Fish adding the fourth goal. Half-time: Warrington '2O points ; Huddersfield 3. On changing ends, Hudders- field put up a bold front for the first ten minutes, and good work was done by Ainley and Jagger. The attack was beaten of, and Fish opmgd the scoring by placing a penalty goal. Fish was again to the fore with try after a good run, and another piece of combination led up to Taylor crossing, and Fish adding his sixth goal. Isherwood made another opening for his captain, who added another goal and a try. Near the close Warring- ton once more asserted themselves. Jordan crossed, and Thomas improved, whilst in the last minute of the game Fish raced in from half way, and converting the try,brought his record up to 30 points for the aftarnoon. Result :—Warrington 10 goals 10 tries (50 points), Huddersfield 1 try (3 points).</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-10-27_WidnesExaminer_art0046" n="art0046">
        <head>COUNTY CHANIPIONSHIP.</head>
        <p>THE COUNTY CHANIPIONSHIP.</p>
        <p>LANCASIIIRE V. YORKSIIME.—A meeting of the Lancashire County Union Committee was held in Man- chester on Tut -day evening. In connection w :th the county championship, the Lancashire team to meet Yorkshire on the Salford ground on Saturday,November 3rd, was electA rs follows :—H. Gifford (Barrow), full back ; J. Leytham (Wigan), left wing, B. Jenkins (Wigan), left centre, R. Wilson (Broughton Rangers) (captain), right centre, and S. Johnson (Leigh), right wing, three-inaher backs; J. Jolley (Runcorn), scrum- mage half, T. White (Oldham), outside half back ; P. O'Neill (Leigh), J. Bentham (Brough- ton Rangers), Di Rees (Salford), A. Naylor (Warrington), R. Padbury (Runcorn), and A. Smith (Oldham), forwards. Reserves : W. Dixon Swinton), full back ; J. Fish (Warrington), left wing, , D. Isherwood (Warrinzton),centre,A. Hogg (Broughton Rangers), right wing, three-quarters ; S. Lees (War- rington), scrummage half, J. Thomes (Wigan), outside half back, Bert Avery (Oldt-am, F. Watkins (Wigan), Dan Davies (Swinton), forwards.</p>
      </div>
