        <p>* * Preparations are being made for the new Mayor. The Town Hall Committee has accepted a tender for re-covering the chairs in the Mayor's parlour. Possibly Alderman Bolton's successor may have a taste of his OW?). for chair-coverings. Would it not be better to Wait a week or two and consult W.P.—?</p>
        <p>* * In the window of a small* shop in the Froghall dis- trict appears the notice :—" Beautiful Warrington Society. Window-b -ixes made to order, estimates free." The only other noticeable article in the window is a child's coffin. Passers-by are wondering if the child's coffin is meant as a sample window-box. . .</p>
        <p>* * * It is reckoned (says the " Tatler ") that there are about 300,000 golfers in Great Britain. and that for links, materials, caddies, etc.. the nation's golf bill amounts to £7,000,000 annually. Something like 1300,000 balls are used up every week, which, at an average cost of is. GI, amounts to £37,500 weekly. * * * Ifr. Winston Churchill, analysed" G. 8.5." on -londay in the following metaphorical extravaganza : Mr. Shaw is like a volcano. There, is a great 'lea' of smoke ; there are large clouds of highly inflammable gases ; and there are here and there brilliant electrical flashes. There are also huge volumes of scalding water, and mud and ashes cast up in all directions, and here and there among the mud and ashes of eytravagance and nonsense a piece of Pure gold ready melted from the central fires of ' -truth."</p>
        <p>a , a The Stockton Heath Parochial Committee com- plained to the Cheshire County Council about the occasional flooding of Ellesmere-road. At the meet- ing of the committee this week the Council's reply was read to the effect that the gullies were choked by the dead leaves from the trees which had been planted along the road. Groans from the tree- planters, and smiles from Mr. Whitley greeted the §tatement. Another conviction recorded against the , trees! * . * The Jubilee of the National Temperance League has been celebrated in London this week, and on Tuesday, -MiBB Agile% Weston produced a magnificent testi.nonial for teetotalism from " Well done • wrote as follows : Lord Charles Beresford, who more teetotalism gets [ peg away ! The amongst fin; men of the service . the better for the nation and the State.l have come to the conclusion that tem Perauce men can stay longest r‘ and are the most physically fit. Nearly all crime in i 1-, the navy is associated, directly or indirectly, with t strong drink."</p>
