        <p>WA R. RINGTON PARISH CHURCH. THE SALE OF WORK CONNECTED WITH THE PARISH CHURCH WILL BE HELD IN THE FAIRFIELD SCHOOLS, ON THURSDAY, FRIDAY AND SATURDAY NEXT. NOVEMBER let, 2nd, and 3rd, from 3 p.m. to 10 p.m. Season Tickets is. 65. ; Thursday 3 to 5 p.m.. ls., sto 10 p.m. 65.; Friday 3 to 10 p.m. 61. ; Saturday 3 to 5 p.m. 6d. 5 to 10 p.m. 3d. £4OO is required to extinguish the Debt on S. George's Extension Fund and to help towards new premises for the Men's Bible Class. THE SALE WILL BE OPENED AT 3 P M. EACH DAY. ON THURSDAY, NOVEMBER IST BY MRS. HALL WALKER AND COL HALL WALKER M.P., if possible. ON FRIDAY NOVEMBER 2ND, BY MRS. HENRY IittkENALL. ON SATURDAY, NOVEMBER 3RD, BE THE MAYRORESS. Various Concerts Au.. have been arranged and an Admir- able little FARCE will be acted at 8 p.m. on Friday and on Saturday at 8.30 p.m. by Members of the Training College Staff entitled "OUR PAYING GUEST." The help of all friends is greely desired both in furnishing the Stalls and attending the Sale. Mrs. Willis, The Rectory ; Mrs. James Cralk. Green Bank; Mrs. Samuel Taylor, Manchester Road ; and Ladies Coo- fleeted with the Parlsh.will be glad to receive contributions. Miss Willis and Miss Brookes will also greatly welcome any help towards the Refreshment Stall, and Flowers, Fruit and Produce will much assist the undertaking. F. W. WILLIS. Rector. JAMES CRAIK, smauEL TAYLOR. }Churchwardens.</p>
        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF NY ARRINGTON.- TO HEATING IiNGINERRS. The TOWN HALL, PARKS and BATHS COMMITTER of the Council of the County Borough of Warrington is prepared to REOIDIVII TENDERS for a small BOILER required for heating the Town Hall. Norms of tender, and all further information may be obtained at the office of the Borough Surveyor, Town Hall, on and after 11.1E9DLY the 30th inst., at which place tenders must be delivered on or before 12 o'cloc't noon on Monday the sth day of November addressed to the Chairman Pt the Town Hall, Parks and Baths Committee. The lowest or any tender not necessarily accepted. THOMAS LOINGDIN, 26th Oct. 196. 'Borough Engineer &amp; Surveyor. Borough Engineer and Surveyor's .dlise.</p>
