        <p>A marriage has just been celebrated in Pentredwr, near Llangollen, the bridegroom being in his 80th year. The bride's age was given as 73 years. But she looked more charming than many younger brides have done. Mr. Abe Bailey addressed a large meeting at Kru„rters- dorp advocating the encouragement of immigration with a view to the settling of whites on the land and the employment of whites by the Government and by municipalities in preference to natives. Subsidences are occurin,g at Quarry Bank, St afford. shire. A young couple walking along a lane in the dark fell into a chasm which had opened in th o road • and had to be rescued with ropes.</p>
